From ba817b49700bf82e800b6716658e080d11e4c273 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Berliner <32103696+Styx85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:19:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] rocblas: tune the gfx90c HB TN selection table on gfx90c

The gfx90c logic is derived from the vega10 tables (tuned on 64 CUs).
Tensile picks the nearest table point by Euclidean distance of the raw
sizes, so for skinny N the nearest point is usually one with matching
M/K but a tiny N, e.g. M=6144 N=512 K=2048 -> [6144, 32, 1, 2560] ->
MT32x32x16, 0.6-0.8 TFLOPS on gfx90c (7 CUs) instead of 2.0-2.5 TFLOPS
for the MT128x128 solutions of the same library.

Re-measure every solution of Cijk_Alik_Bljk_HB on gfx90c (Ryzen 5 5600G)
for 756 of the 790 vega10 sizes (<= 200 GFLOP, <= 600 MB) and for a
grid of M, K in {1024 ... 16384} x N in {16 ... 1024} (707 new points),
and store the fastest solution per size. Solutions and kernels are
unchanged; only the ExactLogic table differs.

Gain of the selected solution over the old default across the 1463
sizes: median 1.67x, mean 2.1x, >10% faster on 1018 sizes. llama.cpp HIP prefill
(FP16 hipBLAS GEMMs, Qwen3 Q4_K_M): 0.6B pp512 911 -> 1347 t/s,
pp128 319 -> 813; 1.7B pp512 283 -> 512-555, pp128 143 -> 347.
Perplexity unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
